(window.IND_GITA_V = window.IND_GITA_V || {})[10] = [{"v":1,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":"श्री भगवानुवाच","spp":"before","sa":"भूय एव महाबाहो शृणु मे परमं वचः ।\nयत्तेऽहं प्रीयमाणाय वक्ष्यामि हितकाम्यया ॥","iast":"bhūya eva mahābāho śṛṇu me paramaṃ vacaḥ |\nyatte’haṃ prīyamāṇāya vakṣyāmi hitakāmyayā ||","read":"bhooya eva mahaabaaho shrinu me paramam vachah |\nyatte'ham preeyamaanaaya vakshyaami hitakaamyayaa ||","spli":"śrī bhagavānuvāca","splr":"shree bhagavaanuvaacha","en":"The Blessed Lord said: Again, O mighty-armed, hear thou My supreme word, that, desiring thy welfare, I will declare to thee who art beloved.","en2":"Again, O mighty-armed, do thou listen to My supreme word, which I, wishing thy welfare, will tell thee who art delighted (to hear Me).","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna asks mighty Arjuna to listen once more to his highest word. He will tell it because he wishes Arjuna well."},{"v":2,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"न मे विदुः सुरगणाः प्रभवं न महर्षयः ।\nअहमादिर्हि देवानां महर्षीणां च सर्वशः ॥","iast":"na me viduḥ suragaṇāḥ prabhavaṃ na maharṣayaḥ |\nahamādirhi devānāṃ maharṣīṇāṃ ca sarvaśaḥ ||","read":"na me viduh suraganaah prabhavam na maharshayah |\nahamaadirhi devaanaam maharsheenaam cha sarvashah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The multitude of the Shining Ones, or the great Rishis, know not my forthcoming, for I am the beginning of all the Shining Ones and the great Rishis.","en2":"Neither the hosts of Devas, nor the great Rishis, know My origin, for in every way I am the source of all the Devas and the great Rishis.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that neither the crowds of Shining Ones nor the great sages know where he comes from, because he is the beginning of them all."},{"v":3,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यो मामजमनादिं च वेत्ति लोकमहेश्वरम् ।\nअसम्मूढः स मर्त्येषु सर्वपापैः प्रमुच्यते ॥","iast":"yo māmajamanādiṃ ca vetti lokamaheśvaram |\nasammūḍhaḥ sa martyeṣu sarvapāpaiḥ pramucyate ||","read":"yo maamajamanaadim cha vetti lokamaheshvaram |\nasammoodhah sa martyeshu sarvapaapaih pramuchyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who knoweth Me, unborn, beginningless, the great Lord of the world, he among mortals without delusion, is liberated from all sin.","en2":"He who knows Me, birthless and beginningless, the great Lord of worlds—he, among mortals, is undeluded, he is freed from all sins.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that whoever knows him as never born, without beginning, the great Lord of the world, is not confused. Among all people, that one is freed from every wrong."},{"v":4,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"बुद्धिर्ज्ञानमसंमोहः क्षमा सत्यं दमः शमः ।\nसुखं दुःखं भवोऽभावो भयं चाभयमेव च ॥","iast":"buddhirjñānamasaṃmohaḥ kṣamā satyaṃ damaḥ śamaḥ |\nsukhaṃ duḥkhaṃ bhavo’bhāvo bhayaṃ cābhayameva ca ||","read":"buddhirjnaanamasammohah kshamaa satyam damah shamah |\nsukham duhkham bhavo'bhaavo bhayam chaabhayameva cha ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Reason, wisdom, non-illusion, forgiveness, truth, self-restraint, calmness, pleasure, pain, existence, non-existence, fear, and also courage","en2":"Intellect, knowledge, non-delusion, forbearance, truth, restraint of the external senses, calmness of heart, happiness, misery, birth, death, fear, as well as fearlessness, non-injury, evenness, contentment, austerity, benevolence, good name, (as well as) ill-fame;—(these) different kinds of qualities of beings arise from Me alone.","en2r":"10.4-5","rv":null,"kid":"Krishna begins a list of the qualities of living beings: understanding, wisdom, freedom from confusion, forgiveness, truth, self-control, calm, happiness and pain, coming to be and ceasing to be, fear and courage."},{"v":5,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अहिंसा समता तुष्टिस्तपो दानं यशोऽयशः ।\nभवन्ति भावा भूतानां मत्त एव पृथग्विधाः ॥","iast":"ahiṃsā samatā tuṣṭistapo dānaṃ yaśo’yaśaḥ |\nbhavanti bhāvā bhūtānāṃ matta eva pṛthagvidhāḥ ||","read":"ahimsaa samataa tushtistapo daanam yasho'yashah |\nbhavanti bhaavaa bhootaanaam matta eva prithagvidhaah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Harmlessness, equanimity, content, austerity, almsgiving, fame and obloquy are the various characteristics of beings issuing from Me.","en2":"Intellect, knowledge, non-delusion, forbearance, truth, restraint of the external senses, calmness of heart, happiness, misery, birth, death, fear, as well as fearlessness, non-injury, evenness, contentment, austerity, benevolence, good name, (as well as) ill-fame;—(these) different kinds of qualities of beings arise from Me alone.","en2r":"10.4-5","rv":null,"kid":"He finishes the list: not harming, evenness, contentment, self-discipline, giving, a good name and a bad name. Krishna says all these different qualities of beings come from him."},{"v":6,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"महर्षयः सप्त पूर्वे चत्वारो मनवस्तथा ।\nमद्भावा मानसा जाता येषां लोक इमाः प्रजाः ॥","iast":"maharṣayaḥ sapta pūrve catvāro manavastathā |\nmadbhāvā mānasā jātā yeṣāṃ loka imāḥ prajāḥ ||","read":"maharshayah sapta poorve chatvaaro manavastathaa |\nmadbhaavaa maanasaa jaataa yeshaam loka imaah prajaah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The seven great Rishis, the ancient Four, and also the Manus, were born of My nature, and mind; of them this race was generated.","en2":"The seven great Rishis as well as the four ancient Manus, possessed of powers like Me (due to their thoughts being fixed on Me), were born of (My) mind; from them are these creatures in the world.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that the seven great sages of old, and the Manus, were born from his mind. All the creatures in the world came from them."},{"v":7,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"एतां विभूतिं योगं च मम यो वेत्ति तत्त्वतः ।\nसोऽविकम्पेन योगेन युज्यते नात्र संशयः ॥","iast":"etāṃ vibhūtiṃ yogaṃ ca mama yo vetti tattvataḥ |\nso’vikampena yogena yujyate nātra saṃśayaḥ ||","read":"etaam vibhootim yogam cha mama yo vetti tattvatah |\nso'vikampena yogena yujyate naatra samshayah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who knows in essence that sovereignty and yoga of Mine, he is harmonised by unfaltering yoga; there is no doubt thereof.","en2":"He who in reality knows these manifold manifestations of My being and (this) Yoga power of Mine, becomes established in the unshakable Yoga; there is no doubt about it.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that whoever truly knows his greatness and his power becomes steady in a way that never wavers. There is no doubt about it."},{"v":8,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अहं सर्वस्य प्रभवो मत्तः सर्वं प्रवर्तते ।\nइति मत्वा भजन्ते मां बुधा भावसमन्विताः ॥","iast":"ahaṃ sarvasya prabhavo mattaḥ sarvaṃ pravartate |\niti matvā bhajante māṃ budhā bhāvasamanvitāḥ ||","read":"aham sarvasya prabhavo mattah sarvam pravartate |\niti matvaa bhajante maam budhaa bhaavasamanvitaah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"I am the Generator of all; all evolves from Me; understanding thus, the wise adore Me in rapt emotion.","en2":"l am the origin of all, from Me everything evolves;—thus thinking the wise worship Me with loving consciousness.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says he is the source of everything, and everything grows from him. The wise know this, and they worship him with deep and loving hearts."},{"v":9,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"मच्चित्ता मद्गतप्राणा बोधयन्तः परस्परम् ।\nकथयन्तश्च मां नित्यं तुष्यन्ति च रमन्ति च ॥","iast":"maccittā madgataprāṇā bodhayantaḥ parasparam |\nkathayantaśca māṃ nityaṃ tuṣyanti ca ramanti ca ||","read":"machchittaa madgatapraanaa bodhayantah parasparam |\nkathayantashcha maam nityam tushyanti cha ramanti cha ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Mindful of Me, their life hidden in Me, illumining each other, ever conversing about Me, they are content and joyful.","en2":"With their minds wholly in Me, with their senses absorbed in Me, enlightening one another, and always speaking of Me, they are satisfied and delighted.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says the wise keep their minds on him and their lives in him. They help each other understand, always talk about him, and are happy and content."},{"v":10,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तेषां सततयुक्तानां भजतां प्रीतिपूर्वकम् ।\nददामि बुद्धियोगं तं येन मामुपयान्ति ते ॥","iast":"teṣāṃ satatayuktānāṃ bhajatāṃ prītipūrvakam |\ndadāmi buddhiyogaṃ taṃ yena māmupayānti te ||","read":"teshaam satatayuktaanaam bhajataam preetipoorvakam |\ndadaami buddhiyogam tam yena maamupayaanti te ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"To these, ever harmonious, worshipping in love, I give the yoga of discrimination by which they come unto Me.","en2":"To them, ever steadfast and serving Me with affection, I give that Buddhi Yoga by which they come unto Me.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that to these people, who are always steady and worship him with love, he gives the gift of clear understanding, by which they come to him."},{"v":11,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तेषामेवानुकम्पार्थमहमज्ञानजं तमः ।\nनाशयाम्यात्मभावस्थो ज्ञानदीपेन भास्वता ॥","iast":"teṣāmevānukampārthamahamajñānajaṃ tamaḥ |\nnāśayāmyātmabhāvastho jñānadīpena bhāsvatā ||","read":"teshaamevaanukampaarthamahamajnaanajam tamah |\nnaashayaamyaatmabhaavastho jnaanadeepena bhaasvataa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Out of pure compassion for them, dwelling within their Self, I destroy the ignorance-born darkness by the shining lamp of wisdom.","en2":"Out of mere compassion for them, [paragraph continues] I, abiding in their hearts, destroy the darkness (in them) born of ignorance, by the luminous lamp of knowledge.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that out of pure kindness he lives in their hearts. With the shining lamp of wisdom, he destroys the darkness that comes from not knowing."},{"v":12,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":"अर्जुन उवाच","spp":"before","sa":"परं ब्रह्म परं धाम पवित्रं परमं भवान् ।\nपुरुषं शाश्वतं दिव्यमादिदेवमजं विभुम् ॥","iast":"paraṃ brahma paraṃ dhāma pavitraṃ paramaṃ bhavān |\npuruṣaṃ śāśvataṃ divyamādidevamajaṃ vibhum ||","read":"param brahma param dhaama pavitram paramam bhavaan |\npurusham shaashvatam divyamaadidevamajam vibhum ||","spli":"arjuna uvāca","splr":"arjuna uvaacha","en":"Arjuna said: Thou art the supreme Eternal, the supreme Abode, the supreme Purity, eternal divine man, primeval Deity, unborn, the Lord!","en2":"The Supreme Brahman, the Supreme Abode, the Supreme Purifier, art Thou. All the Rishis, the Deva-Rishi Nârada as well as Asita, Devala and Vyâsa have declared Thee as the Eternal, the Self-luminous Purusha, the first Deva, Birth-less and All-pervading. So also Thou Thyself sayest to me.","en2r":"10.12-13","rv":null,"kid":"Arjuna praises Krishna. He calls Krishna the highest, the highest home and the highest purity, eternal and divine, the very first, never born, and the Lord."},{"v":13,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"आहुस्त्वामृषयः सर्वे देवर्षिर्नारदस्तथा ।\nअसितो देवलो व्यासः स्वयं चैव ब्रवीषि मे ॥","iast":"āhustvāmṛṣayaḥ sarve devarṣirnāradastathā |\nasito devalo vyāsaḥ svayaṃ caiva bravīṣi me ||","read":"aahustvaamrishayah sarve devarshirnaaradastathaa |\nasito devalo vyaasah svayam chaiva braveeshi me ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"All the Rishis have thus acclaimed Thee, as also the divine Rishi, Nârada; so Asita, Devala, and Vyâsa; and now Thou Thyself tellest it me.","en2":"The Supreme Brahman, the Supreme Abode, the Supreme Purifier, art Thou. All the Rishis, the Deva-Rishi Nârada as well as Asita, Devala and Vyâsa have declared Thee as the Eternal, the Self-luminous Purusha, the first Deva, Birth-less and All-pervading. So also Thou Thyself sayest to me.","en2r":"10.12-13","rv":null,"kid":"Arjuna says that all the great sages have spoken of Krishna this way, and so have Asita and Devala and others. Now Krishna tells him the same thing himself."},{"v":14,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सर्वमेतदृतं मन्ये यन्मां वदसि केशव ।\nन हि ते भगवन् व्यक्तिं विदुर्देवा न दानवाः ॥","iast":"sarvametadṛtaṃ manye yanmāṃ vadasi keśava |\nna hi te bhagavan vyaktiṃ vidurdevā na dānavāḥ ||","read":"sarvametadritam manye yanmaam vadasi keshava |\nna hi te bhagavan vyaktim vidurdevaa na daanavaah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"All this I believe true that Thou sayest to me, O Keshava. Thy manifestation, O Blessed Lord, neither Shining Ones nor Dânavas comprehend.","en2":"I regard all this that Thou sayest to me as true, O Keshava. Verily, O Bhagavân, neither the Devas nor the Dânavas know Thy manifestation.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Arjuna tells Krishna that he believes everything Krishna says is true. He says that not even the Shining Ones, nor other mighty beings, understand how Krishna shows himself."},{"v":15,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"स्वयमेवात्मनाऽत्मानं वेत्थ त्वं पुरुषोत्तम ।\nभूतभावन भूतेश देवदेव जगत्पते ॥","iast":"svayamevātmanā’tmānaṃ vettha tvaṃ puruṣottama |\nbhūtabhāvana bhūteśa devadeva jagatpate ||","read":"svayamevaatmanaa'tmaanam vettha tvam purushottama |\nbhootabhaavana bhootesha devadeva jagatpate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Thyself indeed knowest Thyself by Thyself, O Purushottama; Source of beings, Lord of beings, Shining One of Shining Ones, Ruler of the world!","en2":"Verily, Thou Thyself knowest Thyself by Thyself, O Purusha Supreme, O Source of beings, O Lord of beings, O Deva of Devas, O Ruler of the world.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Arjuna says that only Krishna knows himself, by himself. He calls Krishna the source of beings, the Lord of beings, the Shining One of Shining Ones and the ruler of the world."},{"v":16,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"वक्तुमर्हस्यशेषेण दिव्या ह्यात्मविभूतयः ।\nयाभिर्विभूतिभिर्लोकानिमांस्त्वं व्याप्य तिष्ठसि ॥","iast":"vaktumarhasyaśeṣeṇa divyā hyātmavibhūtayaḥ |\nyābhirvibhūtibhirlokānimāṃstvaṃ vyāpya tiṣṭhasi ||","read":"vaktumarhasyasheshena divyaa hyaatmavibhootayah |\nyaabhirvibhootibhirlokaanimaamstvam vyaapya tishthasi ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Deign to tell without reserve of Thine own divine glories, by which glories Thou remainest, pervading these worlds.","en2":"Thou shouldst indeed speak, without reserve, of Thy divine attributes by which, filling all these worlds, Thou existest.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Arjuna asks Krishna to tell him fully about his divine glories, the glories by which Krishna fills all these worlds and remains in them."},{"v":17,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"कथं विद्यामहं योगिंस्त्वां सदा परिचिन्तयन् ।\nकेषु केषु च भावेषु चिन्त्योऽसि भगवन्मया ॥","iast":"kathaṃ vidyāmahaṃ yogiṃstvāṃ sadā paricintayan |\nkeṣu keṣu ca bhāveṣu cintyo’si bhagavanmayā ||","read":"katham vidyaamaham yogimstvaam sadaa parichintayan |\nkeshu keshu cha bhaaveshu chintyo'si bhagavanmayaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"How may I know thee, O Yogi, by constant meditation? In what, in what aspects art Thou to be thought of by me, O blessed Lord?","en2":"How shall I, O Yogin, meditate ever to know Thee? In what things, Bhagavân, art Thou to be thought of by me?","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Arjuna asks how he can come to know Krishna by thinking of him always. In which things, he asks, should he think of Krishna?"},{"v":18,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"विस्तरेणात्मनो योगं विभूतिं च जनार्दन ।\nभूयः कथय तृप्तिर्हि शृण्वतो नास्ति मेऽमृतम् ॥","iast":"vistareṇātmano yogaṃ vibhūtiṃ ca janārdana |\nbhūyaḥ kathaya tṛptirhi śṛṇvato nāsti me’mṛtam ||","read":"vistarenaatmano yogam vibhootim cha janaardana |\nbhooyah kathaya triptirhi shrinvato naasti me'mritam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"In detail tell me again of Thy yoga and glory, O Janardana; for me there is never satiety in hearing thy life-giving words.","en2":"Speak to me again in detail, Jnanârdana, of Thy Yoga-powers and attributes; for I am never satiated in hearing the ambrosia (of Thy speech).","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Arjuna asks Krishna to tell him again, in detail, about his power and glory. He says he can never hear enough of the life-giving words Krishna speaks."},{"v":19,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":"श्री भगवानुवाच","spp":"before","sa":"हन्त ते कथयिष्यामि दिव्या ह्यात्मविभूतयः ।\nप्राधान्यतः कुरुश्रेष्ठ नास्त्यन्तो विस्तरस्य मे ॥","iast":"hanta te kathayiṣyāmi divyā hyātmavibhūtayaḥ |\nprādhānyataḥ kuruśreṣṭha nāstyanto vistarasya me ||","read":"hanta te kathayishyaami divyaa hyaatmavibhootayah |\npraadhaanyatah kurushreshtha naastyanto vistarasya me ||","spli":"śrī bhagavānuvāca","splr":"shree bhagavaanuvaacha","en":"The Blessed Lord said: Blessed be thou! I will declare to thee My divine glory by its chief characteristics, O best of the Kurus; there is no end to details of Me.","en2":"I shall speak to thee now, O best of the Kurus, of My divine attributes, according to their prominence; there is no end to the particulars of My manifestation.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna, the best of the Kurus, that he will name only the chief of his divine glories, because there is no end to the details."},{"v":20,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अहमात्मा गुडाकेश सर्वभूताशयस्थितः ।\nअहमादिश्च मध्यं च भूतानामन्त एव च ॥","iast":"ahamātmā guḍākeśa sarvabhūtāśayasthitaḥ |\nahamādiśca madhyaṃ ca bhūtānāmanta eva ca ||","read":"ahamaatmaa gudaakesha sarvabhootaashayasthitah |\nahamaadishcha madhyam cha bhootaanaamanta eva cha ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"I, O Gudakesha, am the Self, seated in the heart of all beings; I am the beginning, the middle, and also the end of all beings.","en2":"I am the Self, O Gudâkesha, existent in the heart of all beings; I am the beginning, the middle, and also the end of all beings.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that he is the Self living in the heart of every being. He is the beginning, the middle and the end of all beings."},{"v":21,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"आदित्यानामहं विष्णुर्ज्योतिषां रविरंशुमान् ।\nमरीचिर्मरुतामस्मि नक्षत्राणामहं शशी ॥","iast":"ādityānāmahaṃ viṣṇurjyotiṣāṃ raviraṃśumān |\nmarīcirmarutāmasmi nakṣatrāṇāmahaṃ śaśī ||","read":"aadityaanaamaham vishnurjyotishaam raviramshumaan |\nmareechirmarutaamasmi nakshatraanaamaham shashee ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Of the Adityas I am Vishnu; of radiances the glorious sun; I am Marîchi of the Maruts; of the asterisms the Moon am I.","en2":"Of the Adityas, I am Vishnu; of luminaries, the radiant Sun; of the winds, I am Marichi; of the asterisms, the Moon.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that among the Adityas he is Vishnu, and among lights he is the bright sun. He is Marichi among the winds, and the Moon among the stars."},{"v":22,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"वेदानां सामवेदोऽस्मि देवानामस्मि वासवः ।\nइन्द्रियाणां मनश्चास्मि भूतानामस्मि चेतना ॥","iast":"vedānāṃ sāmavedo’smi devānāmasmi vāsavaḥ |\nindriyāṇāṃ manaścāsmi bhūtānāmasmi cetanā ||","read":"vedaanaam saamavedo'smi devaanaamasmi vaasavah |\nindriyaanaam manashchaasmi bhootaanaamasmi chetanaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Of the Vedas I am the Sâma-Veda; I am Vâsava of the Shining Ones; and of the senses I am the mind; I am of living beings the intelligence.","en2":"I am the Sâma-Veda of the Vedas, and Vâsava (Indra) of the gods; of the senses I am Manas, and intelligence in living beings am I.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that among the Vedas he is one special Veda, and among the gods he is Indra. Of the senses he is the mind, and in living beings he is understanding."},{"v":23,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"रुद्राणां शङ्करश्चास्मि वित्तेशो यक्षरक्षसाम् ।\nवसूनां पावकश्चास्मि मेरुः शिखरिणामहम् ॥","iast":"rudrāṇāṃ śaṅkaraścāsmi vitteśo yakṣarakṣasām |\nvasūnāṃ pāvakaścāsmi meruḥ śikhariṇāmaham ||","read":"rudraanaam shankarashchaasmi vittesho yaksharakshasaam |\nvasoonaam paavakashchaasmi meruh shikharinaamaham ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"And of the Rudras Shañkara am I; Vittesha of the Yakshas and Râkshasas; and of the Vasus I am Pâvaka; Meru of high mountains am I.","en2":"And of the Rudras I am Sankara, of the Yakshas and Râkshasas the Lord of wealth (Kuvera), of the Vasus I am Pâvaka, and of mountains, Meru am I.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that of the Rudras he is Sankara, and of the Yakshas he is Kuvera, the lord of wealth. He is Meru among the high mountains."},{"v":24,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"पुरोधसां च मुख्यं मां विद्धि पार्थ बृहस्पतिम् ।\nसेनानीनामहं स्कन्दः सरसामस्मि सागरः ॥","iast":"purodhasāṃ ca mukhyaṃ māṃ viddhi pārtha bṛhaspatim |\nsenānīnāmahaṃ skandaḥ sarasāmasmi sāgaraḥ ||","read":"purodhasaam cha mukhyam maam viddhi paartha brihaspatim |\nsenaaneenaamaham skandah sarasaamasmi saagarah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"And know Me, O Pârtha, of household priests the chief, Brihaspati: of generals I am Skanda; of lakes I am the ocean.","en2":"And of priests, O son of Prithâ, know Me the chief, Brihaspati; of generals, I am Skanda; of bodies of water, I am the ocean.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that of priests he is the chief, Brihaspati. He is Skanda among army leaders, and the ocean among all the waters."},{"v":25,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"महर्षीणां भृगुरहं गिरामस्म्येकमक्षरम् ।\nयज्ञानां जपयज्ञोऽस्मि स्थावराणां हिमालयः ॥","iast":"maharṣīṇāṃ bhṛgurahaṃ girāmasmyekamakṣaram |\nyajñānāṃ japayajño’smi sthāvarāṇāṃ himālayaḥ ||","read":"maharsheenaam bhriguraham giraamasmyekamaksharam |\nyajnaanaam japayajno'smi sthaavaraanaam himaalayah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Of the great Rishis Bhṛigu; of speech I am the one syllable; of sacrifices I am the sacrifice of silent repetitions; of immovable things the Himâlaya.","en2":"Of the great Rishis I am Bhrigu; of words I am the one syllable \"Om\"; of Yajnas I am the Yajna of Japa (silent repetition); of immovable things the Himâlaya.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that of the great sages he is Bhrigu, and of words he is the one syllable. He is quiet, repeated prayer among offerings, and the mighty mountains among things that never move."},{"v":26,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अश्वत्थः सर्ववृक्षाणां देवर्षीणां च नारदः ।\nगन्धर्वाणां चित्ररथः सिद्धानां कपिलो मुनिः ॥","iast":"aśvatthaḥ sarvavṛkṣāṇāṃ devarṣīṇāṃ ca nāradaḥ |\ngandharvāṇāṃ citrarathaḥ siddhānāṃ kapilo muniḥ ||","read":"ashvatthah sarvavrikshaanaam devarsheenaam cha naaradah |\ngandharvaanaam chitrarathah siddhaanaam kapilo munih ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Asvattha of all tree; and of divine Rishis Nârada; of Gandharvas Chitraratha; of the perfected the Muni Kapila.","en2":"Of all trees (I am) the Ashvattha, and Nârada of Deva-Rishis; Chitraratha of Gandharvas am I, and the Muni Kapila of the perfected ones.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that of all trees he is the Asvattha. He is Chitraratha among the Gandharvas, and the sage Kapila among the perfected ones."},{"v":27,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"उच्चैःश्रवसमश्वानां विद्धि माममृतोद्भवम् ।\nऐरावतं गजेन्द्राणां नराणां च नराधिपम् ॥","iast":"uccaiḥśravasamaśvānāṃ viddhi māmamṛtodbhavam |\nairāvataṃ gajendrāṇāṃ narāṇāṃ ca narādhipam ||","read":"uchchaihshravasamashvaanaam viddhi maamamritodbhavam |\nairaavatam gajendraanaam naraanaam cha naraadhipam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Uchchaishravas of horses know me, nectar-born; Airâvata of lordly elephants, and of men the Monarch.","en2":"Know Me among horses as Uchchaisshravas, Amrita-born; of lordly elephants Airâvata, and of men the king.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna to know him as Uchchaishravas among horses, born from nectar. He is one special elephant among the lordly elephants, and the king among men."},{"v":28,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"आयुधानामहं वज्रं धेनूनामस्मि कामधुक् ।\nप्रजनश्चास्मि कन्दर्पः सर्पाणामस्मि वासुकिः ॥","iast":"āyudhānāmahaṃ vajraṃ dhenūnāmasmi kāmadhuk |\nprajanaścāsmi kandarpaḥ sarpāṇāmasmi vāsukiḥ ||","read":"aayudhaanaamaham vajram dhenoonaamasmi kaamadhuk |\nprajanashchaasmi kandarpah sarpaanaamasmi vaasukih ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Of weapons I am the thunderbolt; of cows I am Kâmadhuk; I am Kandarpa of the progenitors; of serpents Vâsuki am I.","en2":"Of weapons I am the thunderbolt, of cows I am Kâmadhuk; I am the Kandarpa, the cause of offspring; of serpents I am Vâsuki.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that of weapons he is the thunderbolt, and he is Kandarpa, who brings children into being. He is also one special cow, and one special serpent."},{"v":29,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अनन्तश्चास्मि नागानां वरुणो यादसामहम् ।\nपितॄणामर्यमा चास्मि यमः संयमतामहम् ॥","iast":"anantaścāsmi nāgānāṃ varuṇo yādasāmaham |\npitṝṇāmaryamā cāsmi yamaḥ saṃyamatāmaham ||","read":"anantashchaasmi naagaanaam varuno yaadasaamaham |\npitreenaamaryamaa chaasmi yamah samyamataamaham ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"And I am Ananta of Nâgas, Varuna of sea-dwellers I; and of ancestors Aryaman; Yama of governors am I.","en2":"And Ananta of snakes I am, I am Varuna of water-beings; and Aryaman of Pitris I am, I am Yama of controllers.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that of snakes he is Ananta, of the beings of the water he is Varuna, of the ancestors he is Aryaman, and of those who rule and control he is Yama."},{"v":30,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"प्रह्लादश्चास्मि दैत्यानां कालः कलयतामहम् ।\nमृगाणां च मृगेन्द्रोऽहं वैनतेयश्च पक्षिणाम् ॥","iast":"prahlādaścāsmi daityānāṃ kālaḥ kalayatāmaham |\nmṛgāṇāṃ ca mṛgendro’haṃ vainateyaśca pakṣiṇām ||","read":"prahlaadashchaasmi daityaanaam kaalah kalayataamaham |\nmrigaanaam cha mrigendro'ham vainateyashcha pakshinaam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"And I am Prahlâda of Daityas; of calculators Time am I; and of wild beasts I the imperial beast; and Vainateya of birds.","en2":"And Prahlâda am I of Diti's progeny, of measurers I am Time; and of beasts I am the lord of beasts, and Garuda of birds.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that of all that counts and measures he is Time. He is the lord of beasts among wild animals, and Garuda among birds."},{"v":31,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"पवनः पवतामस्मि रामः शस्त्रभृतामहम् ।\nझषाणां मकरश्चास्मि स्रोतसामस्मि जाह्नवी ॥","iast":"pavanaḥ pavatāmasmi rāmaḥ śastrabhṛtāmaham |\njhaṣāṇāṃ makaraścāsmi srotasāmasmi jāhnavī ||","read":"pavanah pavataamasmi raamah shastrabhritaamaham |\njhashaanaam makarashchaasmi srotasaamasmi jaahnavee ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Of purifiers I am the wind; Rama of warriors I; and I am Makara of fishes; of streams the Gangâ am I.","en2":"Of purifiers I am the wind, Râma of warriors am I; of fishes I am the shark, of streams I am Jâhnavi (the Ganges).","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that of things that make clean he is the wind, and of warriors he is Rama. He is the shark among fishes, and the Ganges among rivers."},{"v":32,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सर्गाणामादिरन्तश्च मध्यं चैवाहमर्जुन ।\nअध्यात्मविद्या विद्यानां वादः प्रवदतामहम् ॥","iast":"sargāṇāmādirantaśca madhyaṃ caivāhamarjuna |\nadhyātmavidyā vidyānāṃ vādaḥ pravadatāmaham ||","read":"sargaanaamaadirantashcha madhyam chaivaahamarjuna |\nadhyaatmavidyaa vidyaanaam vaadah pravadataamaham ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Of creations the beginning and the ending, and also the middle am I, O Arjuna. Of sciences the science concerning the Self; the speech of orators I.","en2":"Of manifestations I, am the beginning, the middle and also the end; of all knowledges I am the knowledge of the Self, and Vâda of disputants.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that he is the beginning, the middle and the end of all that is made. Of all knowledge he is knowing the Self, and he is the speech of those who debate."},{"v":33,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अक्षराणामकारोऽस्मि द्वन्द्वः सामासिकस्य च ।\nअहमेवाक्षयः कालो धाताऽहं विश्वतोमुखः ॥","iast":"akṣarāṇāmakāro’smi dvandvaḥ sāmāsikasya ca |\nahamevākṣayaḥ kālo dhātā’haṃ viśvatomukhaḥ ||","read":"aksharaanaamakaaro'smi dvandvah saamaasikasya cha |\nahamevaakshayah kaalo dhaataa'ham vishvatomukhah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Of letters the letter A I am, and the duality of a compound; I also everlasting Time; I the Supporter, whose face turns everywhere.","en2":"Of letters the letter A am I, and Dvandva of all compounds; I alone am the inexhaustible Time, I the Sustainer (by dispensing fruits of actions) All-formed.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that of letters he is the letter A, and of joined words he is the pair. He is endless Time, and the one who holds up all, facing every way."},{"v":34,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"मृत्युः सर्वहरश्चाहमुद्भवश्च भविष्यताम् ।\nकीर्तिः श्रीर्वाक्च नारीणां स्मृतिर्मेधा धृतिः क्षमा ॥","iast":"mṛtyuḥ sarvaharaścāhamudbhavaśca bhaviṣyatām |\nkīrtiḥ śrīrvākca nārīṇāṃ smṛtirmedhā dhṛtiḥ kṣamā ||","read":"mrityuh sarvaharashchaahamudbhavashcha bhavishyataam |\nkeertih shreervaakcha naareenaam smritirmedhaa dhritih kshamaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"And all-devouring Death am I, and the origin of all to come; and of feminine qualities, fame, prosperity, speech, memory, intelligence, constancy, forgiveness.","en2":"And I am the all-seizing Death, and the prosperity of those who are to be prosperous; of the feminine qualities (I am) Fame, Prosperity (or beauty), Inspiration, Memory, Intelligence, Constancy and Forbearance.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says he is Death, which takes all. He says that among the feminine qualities he is fame, good fortune, memory, understanding, steadiness and patient forgiveness."},{"v":35,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"बृहत्साम तथा साम्नां गायत्री छन्दसामहम् ।\nमासानां मार्गशीर्षोऽहमृतूनां कुसुमाकरः ॥","iast":"bṛhatsāma tathā sāmnāṃ gāyatrī chandasāmaham |\nmāsānāṃ mārgaśīrṣo’hamṛtūnāṃ kusumākaraḥ ||","read":"brihatsaama tathaa saamnaam gaayatree chhandasaamaham |\nmaasaanaam maargasheersho'hamritoonaam kusumaakarah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Of hymns also Brihatsâman; Gâyatrî of metres am I; of months I am Mârgasîrsha; of seasons the flowery.","en2":"Of Sâmas also I am the Brihat-Sâma, of metres Gâyatri am I; of months I am Mârgashirsha, of seasons the flowery season.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna names himself as one special hymn, one pattern of verse and one month. He says that of the seasons he is the season of flowers."},{"v":36,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"द्यूतं छलयतामस्मि तेजस्तेजस्विनामहम् ।\nजयोऽस्मि व्यवसायोऽस्मि सत्त्वं सत्त्ववतामहम् ॥","iast":"dyūtaṃ chalayatāmasmi tejastejasvināmaham |\njayo’smi vyavasāyo’smi sattvaṃ sattvavatāmaham ||","read":"dyootam chhalayataamasmi tejastejasvinaamaham |\njayo'smi vyavasaayo'smi sattvam sattvavataamaham ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"I am the gambling of the cheat, and the splendour of splendid things I; I am victory, I am determination, and the truth of the truthful I.","en2":"I am the gambling of the fraudulent, I am the power of the powerful; I am victory, I am effort, I am Sattva of the Sâttvika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says he is the gambling of the cheat, and the greatness of the great. He is victory, he is firm effort, and he is the goodness of the good."},{"v":37,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"वृष्णीनां वासुदेवोऽस्मि पाण्डवानां धनंजयः ।\nमुनीनामप्यहं व्यासः कवीनामुशना कविः ॥","iast":"vṛṣṇīnāṃ vāsudevo’smi pāṇḍavānāṃ dhanaṃjayaḥ |\nmunīnāmapyahaṃ vyāsaḥ kavīnāmuśanā kaviḥ ||","read":"vrishneenaam vaasudevo'smi paandavaanaam dhanamjayah |\nmuneenaamapyaham vyaasah kaveenaamushanaa kavih ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Of the Vṛishnis Vâsudeva am I; of the Pândavas Dhananjaya; of the Sages also I am Vyâsa; of poets Ushanâ the Bard.","en2":"Of the Vrishnis I am Vâsudeva; of the Pândavas, Dhananjaya; and also of the Munis I am Vyâsa; of the sages, Ushanas the sage.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna goes on naming himself in each group. He names one of the Vrishnis, a great sage among sages, and Ushanas among poets. He also says he is Dhananjaya."},{"v":38,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"दण्डो दमयतामस्मि नीतिरस्मि जिगीषताम् ।\nमौनं चैवास्मि गुह्यानां ज्ञानं ज्ञानवतामहम् ॥","iast":"daṇḍo damayatāmasmi nītirasmi jigīṣatām |\nmaunaṃ caivāsmi guhyānāṃ jñānaṃ jñānavatāmaham ||","read":"dando damayataamasmi neetirasmi jigeeshataam |\nmaunam chaivaasmi guhyaanaam jnaanam jnaanavataamaham ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Of rulers I am the sceptre; of those that seek victory I am statesmanship; and of secrets I am also silence; the knowledge of knowers am I.","en2":"Of punishers I am the sceptre; of those who seek to conquer, I am statesmanship; and also of things secret I am silence, and the knowledge of knowers am I.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that of rulers he is the sceptre, and of those who seek to win he is wise leadership. He is silence among secrets, and the knowledge of those who know."},{"v":39,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यच्चापि सर्वभूतानां बीजं तदहमर्जुन ।\nन तदस्ति विना यत्स्यान्मया भूतं चराचरम् ॥","iast":"yaccāpi sarvabhūtānāṃ bījaṃ tadahamarjuna |\nna tadasti vinā yatsyānmayā bhūtaṃ carācaram ||","read":"yachchaapi sarvabhootaanaam beejam tadahamarjuna |\nna tadasti vinaa yatsyaanmayaa bhootam charaacharam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"And whatsoever is the seed of all beings, that am I, O Arjuna; nor is there aught, moving or unmoving, that may exist bereft of Me.","en2":"And whatsoever is the seed of all beings, that also am I, O Arjuna. There is no being, whether moving or unmoving, that can exist without Me.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that he is the seed of all beings. Nothing at all, moving or still, can exist without him."},{"v":40,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"नान्तोऽस्ति मम दिव्यानां विभूतीनां परंतप ।\nएष तूद्देशतः प्रोक्तो विभूतेर्विस्तरो मया ॥","iast":"nānto’sti mama divyānāṃ vibhūtīnāṃ paraṃtapa |\neṣa tūddeśataḥ prokto vibhūtervistaro mayā ||","read":"naanto'sti mama divyaanaam vibhooteenaam paramtapa |\nesha tooddeshatah prokto vibhootervistaro mayaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"There is no end of My divine powers, O Parantapa. What has been declared is illustrative of My infinite glory.","en2":"There is no end of My divine attributes, O scorcher of foes; but this is a brief statement by Me of the particulars of My divine attributes.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says there is no end to his divine powers. What he has told is only a small part, a few examples of his endless glory."},{"v":41,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यद्यद्विभूतिमत्सत्त्वं श्रीमदूर्जितमेव वा ।\nतत्तदेवावगच्छ त्वं मम तेजोंऽशसंभवम् ॥","iast":"yadyadvibhūtimatsattvaṃ śrīmadūrjitameva vā |\ntattadevāvagaccha tvaṃ mama tejoṃ’śasaṃbhavam ||","read":"yadyadvibhootimatsattvam shreemadoorjitameva vaa |\ntattadevaavagachchha tvam mama tejom'shasambhavam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Whatsoever is glorious, good, beautiful, and mighty, understand thou that to go forth from a fragment of My splendour.","en2":"Whatever being there is great, prosperous or powerful, that know thou to be a product of a part of My splendour.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that whatever is glorious and mighty comes from just a small part of his splendour."},{"v":42,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अथवा बहुनैतेन किं ज्ञातेन तवार्जुन ।\nविष्टभ्याहमिदं कृत्स्नमेकांशेन स्थितो जगत् ॥","iast":"athavā bahunaitena kiṃ jñātena tavārjuna |\nviṣṭabhyāhamidaṃ kṛtsnamekāṃśena sthito jagat ||","read":"athavaa bahunaitena kim jnaatena tavaarjuna |\nvishtabhyaahamidam kritsnamekaamshena sthito jagat ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"But what is the knowledge of all these details to thee, O Arjuna? Having pervaded this whole universe with one fragment of Myself, I remain.","en2":"Or what avails thee to know all this diversity, O Arjuna? (Know thou this,. that) I exist, supporting this whole world by a portion of Myself.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna asks Arjuna what use all these details are to him. Krishna fills and holds up this whole universe with just one small part of himself, and he remains."}];
